mulation and synchronization\nPLAN.md:231:## 10. Implementation shape and packaging\nPLAN.md:269:## 11. Build sequence and decision gates\nPLAN.md:273:### Pass 1: Verify contracts and make a real executable\nPLAN.md:279:### Pass 2: Prove shared-world play before full content\nPLAN.md:285:### Pass 3: Finish the complete rules and campaign\nPLAN.md:291:### Pass 4: Complete presentation, input, and tools\nPLAN.md:297:### Pass 5: Verify the delivered artifact and close the brief\nPLAN.md:303:## 12. Verification strategy\nPLAN.md:309:### State and whole-game checks\nPLAN.md:320:### Browser and input checks\nPLAN.md:336:### Audio checks\nPLAN.md:340:### Hosted and standalone networking checks\nPLAN.md:355:### Shared-machine discipline\nPLAN.md:357:Prefer `file://` and engine headless tools. If a server is needed, bind `127.0.0.1` on port zero, capture its assigned port, and verify the served page's game identity before trusting results. Track a [... omitted end of long line]\nPLAN.md:359:## 13. Delivery and completion contract\nPLAN.md:361:Include the four required information groups **both in the final chat reply and in an accessible in-game About/Credits screen**: Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedb [... omitted end of long line]\nPLAN.md:365:Save the builder exit-interview artifact required by your brief with its exact schema, filled source-information object, ordered feedback arrays, and complete AI Hub catalogue object. Parse it with co [... omitted end of long line]\nPLAN.md:380:- No TODO, placeholder, sample launcher, disabled feature masquerading as complete, or unreported material limitation remains.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
