{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('PLAN.md').read_text().splitlines():\n    if any(needle in line for needle in ['Escape literal', 'Stick or keyboard', 'Only hostile movement', 'Opening Dev Mode']):\n        print(repr(line))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"'Only hostile movement and attack clocks slow. Player movement, player shots, UI, audio scheduling, and the authoritative real-time clock continue normally. Boss warning timers affected by the brake must remain aligned with the attack they describe. Ground rollers slow but do not become shootable. This is a slowdown, not a rewind: no restoring dead enemies, reversing score, or duplicating pickups.'\n\"Opening Dev Mode marks a run as modified before any score can be saved. A dedicated test-mode entry may expose stable automation hooks, but Dev Mode itself must be reachable with normal controls. In active hosted play, obey Hub's session controls and disallow shared-state editing, level jumps, restarts, and a local world pause. Offer the full toolbox in standalone solo; expose only safe local presentation settings or read-only inspection during hosted rounds.\"\n'The build must inline the engine, custom art/animation code, game modules, styles, required Hub client, and game-owned content in dependency order. Escape literal `</script` sequences inside embedded JavaScript as `<\\\\/script`, including text in engine comments. Never depend on sibling development files being present beside the final HTML. Permitted external dependencies must be version-pinned and listed in About; copy any necessary runtime assets into the artifact or use deliberate stable remote URLs rather than accidental local module fetches.'\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
